# Folder-local ignore rules for the Azure module.
#
# The repo-root .gitignore already covers terraform.tfvars, tfstate, and
# .terraform/ everywhere. This file exists for the ONE thing it does not
# know about: route53-credentials.env, which holds a live AWS access key
# pair. Keeping the rule here rather than editing the root .gitignore keeps
# the Azure work fully self-contained (see README.md -> Isolation).
#
# Per the license-leak-on-rename lesson in CLAUDE.md, the credential glob is
# deliberately broad rather than an exact filename -- no rename of the
# wildcard portion can re-expose it.

*credentials.env
*credentials*.env
route53-credentials*

# Belt-and-braces duplicates of the root rules, so this folder stays safe
# even if it is ever copied out of the repo and handed to a teammate on its
# own (which is exactly how infra/terraform-subdomain/ is distributed).
terraform.tfvars
graphwise-secrets.yaml
n8n.txt
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
files/licenses/*
!files/licenses/README.txt
